<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39159" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-tollo</span></b> , ĕre,
			v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To stretch forth</i> or <i>out</i>,
				<i>to bring forth</i> (ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 3, 2, 71</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pleiadas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Avien. Arat. 567</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>To prolong</i>, <i>protract</i>, <i>put off</i>, <i>defer</i>, Lucil. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 159, 23</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitam in crastinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 3, 5, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortem sibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 8, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">feturam mulierum non ultra decimum mensem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 3, 16, 15</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>To elevate</i>, <i>raise</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vox a minore solita ad majorem protolli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 31, 7, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
